# Per-step fetch study: unsloth/Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct, base int1, prefill fetch k=128, self-written targets (T=0.7)

31 pauses, 42.6 teacher-forced steps per pause on average (cap 64). Targets: the bf16 model's own next message (sampled at temperature 0.7, seed 0 + per-pause offset; bf16 prefill of history and tool output; 25-64 tokens, mean 42.6), saved in self_targets.jsonl; every row is teacher-forced on them. dNLL in nats per target token against the per-step bf16 row. Base: int1 history, block 16 (SpeCache's modified 1-bit quantizer); block 0, the recent 64 tokens and the trailing partial block are bf16. Tool output prefilled over the int1 history with a per-chunk top-128 fetch (fetch rows; the uniform int1 row and fetch_all_noprefill without); uniform rows over their own precision, the bf16 row over bf16.

## Checks

- bf16 row vs itself: max |dNLL| 0.0e+00
- per-step vs sdpa teacher forcing, NLL difference per pause (the stop criterion): bf16 row max 0.0073 (mean 0.0024), int1 row max 0.0283 (mean 0.0073)
- uniform int1 dNLL, sdpa batched +0.5574 vs per-step +0.5591 (max per-pause |difference| 0.0218)
- largest single-token log-prob difference (reported only): bf16 0.197, int1 0.451
- 80.6 s per pause on average, 41.6 min total
- speculative token (spec rows, guess of each step's input from the real previous token): correct on 86.6% (spec@16), 87.0% (spec@32), 88.0% (spec@64), 88.0% (spec@128), 89.2% (spec@match) of steps
- speculative token (spec_chain rows, SpeCache's chained guess of the next input): correct on 24.5% (spec_chain@16), 31.7% (spec_chain@32), 28.0% (spec_chain@64), 28.2% (spec_chain@128), 28.3% (spec_chain@match) of steps
- k = match: 1,116 tokens per KV head and layer on average (min 495, max 2,110), i.e. int1 + fetched set = int2's memory
